{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2244","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Stepan and Permutation"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Stepan found a permutation $$$p$$$ of length $$$n$$$. Of course, he decided to sort it. To make the process more interesting, he chose two positive integers $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$ $$$(x + y \\le n)$$$ and defined a rule for swapping elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one move, Stepan can choose two indices $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ $$$(1 \\le i, j \\le n)$$$ and swap the elements $$$p_i$$$ and $$$p_j$$$ if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at least one"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the following conditions holds:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$|i - j| = x$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$|i - j| = y$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Stepan wants to know whether it is possible to sort the permutation in ascending order using any number of such operations. Help him answer this question."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ $$$(1 \\le t \\le 10^4)$$$ — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$x$$$, and $$$y$$$ $$$(1 \\le x, y \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$x + y \\le n)$$$ — the length of the array and the numbers chosen by Stepan."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$p_i$$$ $$$(1 \\le p_i \\le n)$$$ — the array $$$p$$$; it is guaranteed that $$$p$$$ is a permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if it is possible to sort the permutation with the given $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$, and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You may output each letter in any case (lowercase or uppercase). For example, the strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be accepted."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n5 2 3\n5 4 3 2 1\n6 2 4\n2 1 4 3 6 5\n4 2 2\n1 2 3 4\n5 2 3\n1 2 3 5 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\nYES\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"2244C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2244/problem/C"}